  "split_rule": "Sort the eight USZ patient ids. First five discovery, last three held out. Not chosen by TLS count or expression.",
  "it_tls_rule": "A TLS focus is hex-connected ground_truth=TLS spots within 1.3 pitches. IT if it touches at least one TUM neighbor and has no NOR neighbor. INFL neighbors are allowed but do not count as tumor. Blank neighbors stay unknown and are not votes.",
  "spots_used": "ground_truth==TUM only. TLS core spots are not relabeled as tumor. Blank labels stay unknown.",
  "distance": "Signed Euclidean um from the focus. Outside spots: distance to nearest focus spot. Focus spots: negative distance to nearest non-focus spot. Curves use tumor spots only, so scaled 0 is the nearest tumor spot, not the core.",
  "scale": "Per TLS, min-max the positive tumor-spot distances to 0-1. Do not pool scaled distances across TLS or patients.",
  "microns_recorded": "For each curve, scaled 0, 0.75 and 1 map back to micrometers on that TLS axis.",
  "score": "AUCell: rank genes by raw count within spot; aucMaxRank = floor(0.05*n_genes); score is the AUC of the gene set in that top rank window.",
  "spline": "Natural cubic spline, df=3, interior knots at the 1/3 and 2/3 quantiles of that TLS scaled distances. Fit AUCell ~ spline(scaled distance) by OLS. Evaluate at 0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75.",
  "shape": "high-to-low if the four fitted values are non-increasing and the drop from 0 to 0.75 is at least 0.02 AUC. low-to-high is the mirror. Otherwise flat/nonmonotonic.",
  "min_spots": "A TLS is evaluable only if it has at least 30 tumor spots and at least 8 tumor spots at scaled distance >= 0.5.",
  "patient_shape": "Majority of that patient evaluable IT TLS. A tie is flat/nonmonotonic.",
  "stability_gate": "Discovery patients only. A named set is concordant if at least 3 evaluable discovery patients have the expected shape, and that count exceeds the opposite shape. High-to-low family passes only if IFN_I, IFN_II, MHC_II and INFLAMMATION all pass. Low-to-high family passes only if G2M and EMT both pass. B-axis, scored the same way, must not be concordant low-to-high. If fewer than 3 discovery patients are evaluable, the field is not stable and inversion does not start.",
  "inversion": "Only if the stability gate passes. Template is the pointwise median of discovery fitted curves on the four grid points. Held-out candidates are tumor spots. Match score is the median Spearman of binned AUCell versus the template across the sets that passed. Predicted center is the argmax. B-axis baseline is the tumor spot with maximum B AUCell. A hit is predicted center within 200 um of the nearest true IT TLS centroid. Success is a higher held-out patient hit count for the field than for B. No spatial p-value is computed.",
